From fc617acd30a461ba2a85e0a4e1d58f30a59f27a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jean-Pascal MEWENEMESSE <pasciano007@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:49:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(stack): read the package manifests correctly and
 carry a notice

Three defects in how build-stack.mjs reads the KuboCD manifests, and one new
field.

Package definition links pointed at `main`. The page is a snapshot: it records
the commits it was generated from, and the footer's "Built from" links use them,
but every per-component link ignored them. JupyterHub already showed 4.3.3-p06
while the linked manifest on main said p07, 72 minutes after #44 merged. The SHA
was in scope at the call site all along.

The `registry:` key was discarded. Bitnami-style charts split the host from the
path, so keycloak.yaml's `registry: quay.io` plus `repository: okdp/sandbox-images/keycloak`
was published as a registry-less path that reads as Docker Hub and 404s there.
Two references were affected. With references now qualified, the bare "okdp/"
entry in OKDP_IMAGE_PREFIXES can go: it only existed to recognise the mangled
form, and was a latent false positive for any real Docker Hub image in an okdp
namespace.

`tag:` was required on the line immediately after `repository:`. Charts routinely
put `pullPolicy:` between them, and five images were dropped silently, including
the Polaris server and the CloudNativePG operator. Two components rendered no
images at all. Intervening keys are now allowed, but never another `repository:`,
so adjacent image blocks cannot be paired across.

Every reference is also normalised to a fully-qualified form, so postgres:16-alpine
becomes docker.io/library/postgres:16-alpine and nothing on the page relies on an
implicit registry.

Finally, a component may carry an optional notice, curated in stack-metadata.yaml
beside the display names, keyed into the locale files. Ingress NGINX uses it.

